                },
                "tldr": "In this article, the authors explore the issues related to the growing federal prison population and propose changes to federal criminal justice policy to reduce the prison population while maintaining public safety, and find that some of the growth is due to changes in federal criminal criminal justice policies during the previous three decades.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "score": 0.5084226,
                "section_names": [
                    "Cost of Operating the Federal Prison System"
                ],
                "rank": 3,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace_full_text",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses detailed BOP cost data to examine operating expenses, budget allocations, and aging inmate impacts; lacks revenue discussion and broader demographic analysis.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Economic analysis of incarceration",
                            "relevance": "Highly Relevant"
