            "relevance_ZwZUXa": "- **Relevance Score:** 58/100\n- **Relevance Tag:** Somewhat Relevant\n- **Reasoning:** Provides detailed daily cost figures for German states and links costs to offense types, but lacks component cost breakdowns, revenue analysis, and extensive demographic cost modeling.",
            "abstract_eTrloI": "Der Beitrag stellt das bundeseinheitliche Schema zur Ermittlung der Tageshaftkosten in den deutschen Bundeslandern vor und liefert einen Uberblick der ausgewiesenen Tageshaftkosten aus dem Haushaltsjahr 2001. Die Bandbreite dieser direkten Kosten liegt zwischen 61,09 Euro pro Hafttag in Bayern und 91,40 Euro in Hamburg. Fur einen ersten Versuch diese gefangnisspezifischen Kosten auf die Kostenverursacher, darunter werden unterschiedliche Straftatengruppen verstanden zu verteilen, dienen Informationen die aus dem amerikanischen Strafvollzug gewonnen werden konnen.",
            "key-financial_HGDnyX": "The paper presents a nationwide scheme for determining daily detention costs in German federal states, providing an overview of reported daily detention costs from the 2001 fiscal year. The range of these direct costs was between 61.09 Euro per day in Bavaria and 91.40 Euro in Hamburg. Information from American corrections is used for an initial attempt to distribute these prison-specific costs to cost generators, understood as different groups of offenses.",
            "demographics_sGfiV7": "Not available in metadata.",
            "cost-data-and_I7WOQt": "The daily incarceration costs in German correctional facilities for the 2001 fiscal year ranged from 61.09 Euro per day in Bavaria to 91.40 Euro per day in Hamburg. The paper presents a unified scheme for determining these daily costs across German states. Information from American corrections is used to distribute these prison-specific costs to different offender groups.",
            "specific-cost_RNUson": "The paper presents daily incarceration costs from the 2001 fiscal year, ranging from 61.09 Euro per day in Bavaria to 91.40 Euro per day in Hamburg. It introduces a Germany-wide scheme for determining these daily costs. Information from American correctional systems is used for an initial attempt to distribute these prison-specific costs among different crime groups. No other specific cost categories, annual costs, operational budgets, healthcare, food, staffing, infrastructure costs, revenue generation, or demographic cost variations are mentioned.",
            "key-economic_rSp2Jg": "Not available in metadata.",
            "demographics_igYX7G": "Not available in metadata."
        },
