                "tldr": "The authors studied the role of labor coercion in fiscal capacity building in Nigeria during the colonial era and found that coerced convict labor made up a significant part of colonial expenditures, and provided new insights on the costs of colonial infrastructure and the effects of the colonial revenue imperative on African populations.",
                "podcast": null,
