                "tldr": "The United States currently incarcerates a higher share of its population than any other country in the world as mentioned in this paper, and a reduction in incarceration rates just to the level we had in 1993 (which was already high by historical standards) would lower correctional expenditures by $16.9 billion per year, with the large majority of these savings accruing to state and local governments.",
