            "abstract_eTrloI": "INTRODUCTION 95 I. BACKGROUND 96 A. Incarceration Rates 96 B. Costs of Incarceration 97 C. Charging Inmates for the Cost of their Incarceration 99 II. LEGISLATION 100 A. State Statutes 100 B. Litigation Regarding the Statutes 104 1. Due Process Challenge 104 III. PAY-TO-STAY PROGRAMS 106 A. Effectiveness of Current Programs 106 B. Criticism of Pay-to-Stay Statutes 108 IV. PENDING LEGISLATION IN NEW YORK AND NEW JERSEY 110 A. New York\u2019s Madoff Bill 110 B. New Jersey Bill 112 V. ALTERNATIVE WAYS TO ADDRESS THE BUDGET DECREASE AND/OR HIGH INCARCERATION RATE ...... 114 A. Jail and Prison Closures 114 B. Reducing Guard to Inmate Ratio 115 C. Releasing Prisoners 116 D. Sentencing Alternatives 117 1. Community Courts 117 2. Drug Programs 118 3. Sentencing Reform 119 E. California\u2019s Pay-to-Stay Jails 120 VI. ANALYSIS OF PAY-TO-STAY LEGISLATION IN NEW YORK AND NEW JERSEY 121",
