                "tldr": "In Prisonomics Vicky Pryce, an economist and former Joint Head of the United Kingdom\u2019s Government Economic Service, identifies many of the costs associated with prison use and argues that incarceration makes inmates more likely to reoffend than do community sentences and treatment, creating additional costs in the future as discussed by the authors.",
                "podcast": null,
