                "tldr": "The United States incarcerates more persons than any other country as discussed by the authors , and older adults constitute the fastest-growing demographic of prisoners (Figure 1) and the geriatric threshold in correctional facilities is age 55 or, in some states, age 50 (Williams et al., 2012).",
